                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                        "entry_id": "60fd7cd2-0741-3609-a048-45dc6d24eb99",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of gorget (“surgical instrument”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "possibly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "216a43e8-8540-48f6-b03f-ba68f8662b1e",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "[…] then placing the Bill which is at the end of the Gorgeret into the Groove of the ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07446a31-df4a-4a48-9908-a3e9cd9cb8ba",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "These, having first made an Incision as before, pass the End of the Gorgeret thro' the Groove of the Catheter into the Bladder, as we directed for the male Conductor :"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3f2725d-cb79-45db-a4b2-69efe3240cc9",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "V. The under part of the double gorgeret separated from the upper, which varies but little in shape from the common gorgeret."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bea980cf-a4be-45bb-820f-1d1107853951",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "I then introduce the beak of the common gorgeret into the groove of the staff, and press, it on, till it gets into the bladder, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3b903dd-17c3-435f-9479-3b3a96831b44",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "I therefore took the double gorgeret, without the cutting blade affixed, intending only to push back the stone, and dilate the neck of the bladder, which I did by getting the beak of the gorgeret into the sulcus of the staff […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc89f6b4-2fec-4277-a266-695881fae654",
                                "sense_id": "d1a6b7fc-092c-3676-94a5-1ff871e35096",
                                "text": "After this method became known, many different forms of gorgets and gorgerets were invented ; which it would answer no useful purpose to describe. Of one of them, Mr. Liston remarks, \"It is more like an instrument for cutting turf, - a 'flauchter-spade,' - than for performing a delicate surgical operation.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
